course: dictionary
lesson: 2240
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and «crack» is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Ask yourself: what would fit here?
explain: «Ice with a crack in it is not safe to walk on.» A crack here is a thin line where the ice has broken but not fallen apart. Check it by swapping in your meaning: a thin line in the ice still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: «Leo cracked the code in ten minutes.» Nobody smashed a code, so to crack a code means to solve it. Phrases like «crack a joke» and «crack the case» work the same way: read the whole phrase, not just one word.
fact: A crack is a thin line where something has broken but not fallen apart.
fact: A crack can also be a narrow gap, as in «the door opened a crack».
fact: A crack can be a sudden, sharp, loud sound, as in «a crack of thunder».
fact: To crack something means to break it so lines appear, or to break it open, as in «crack an egg» or «crack a nut».
fact: «At the crack of dawn» means very early in the morning. To crack a joke means to tell it, and to crack a code means to solve it.
exercise: «The door opened a crack, and a cat peeped in.» What does crack mean here? | *A narrow gap | A line on the glass | A loud bang | A funny story
exercise: «Dad cracked the eggs into the bowl.» What does cracked mean? | Made a loud sound | Solved them like a puzzle | Told them as a joke | *Broke them open
exercise: Ruby says, «I will crack the code.» What does crack the code mean? | To break it into pieces | To freeze it in ice | *To solve it | To tell it as a joke
test: «The capuchin cracks a nut with a stone like a hammer.» What does cracks mean here? | A narrow gap | To tell a joke | *To break something open | A sudden loud sound
test: «Kintsugi shows that cracks can be beautiful.» What is a crack in this sentence? | A joke that makes people laugh | A code that has been solved | *A thin line where something has broken but not fallen apart | A sudden sharp sound
exam: «Ice with a crack in it is not safe to walk on.» What does crack mean here? | To solve a puzzle | *A thin line where something has broken but not fallen apart | A loud sound at the crack of dawn | To tell a joke
